[{"kind":"modules.unused_import","proved":false,"by_law":"an import nothing anywhere reads changes no program it stands over","repaired":false,"edits":[{"before":"use lib.{Other}\n","after":"\n"}],"doc":"A name imported and never used ANYWHERE in its MODULE — never per FILE, since bs2 merges a module's own files into one bundle, so an import in one file may serve another (`program.av`'s import can be `mod.av`'s to use); a per-file scan deletes an import a sibling still depends on. The compiler refuses a MISSING import (F3000) and one a module does not export (F3012); an unused one is silent, so this rule keeps that direction. `unused_imports()`/`unused_import_decls()` (features/code.av, THE REFERENCES RELATION) already exempt a component instance (`DeclFacts.instance`): its use is being REACHABLE for a `collect`, not being read.","docs_cmd":"avra docs modules.unused_import"}]
